# Emitted by crates/particles/build.sh from the compiled WebAssembly. Committed
# so no consumer needs a Rust toolchain, but it is generated rather than
# written — keep it out of diffs, reviews and the language statistics.
src/wasm.ts linguist-generated=true

# Tests are excluded from the language statistics, so the bar describes the
# code the package ships rather than the code that checks it. There is more
# test than source here — 43 cases covering a canvas, an animation loop, a
# pointer and a media query — which says something true about the rigour and
# nothing useful about what the package is.
#
# Not hidden: they are in the tree, in CI, and behind the coverage badge.
# -linguist-detectable is the attribute meant for this; marking them vendored
# or documentation would be filing them as something they are not.
src/*.test.ts -linguist-detectable
